      "shortName": "one-global-control",
      "title": "theme.border_width becomes the one control; 0 means none everywhere",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "Path 1 (Button, Input, Select, Checkbox, Tag, Card via `PaintCx::border()`) is already correct. Path 2 is the problem: `PaintCx::bracket_frame` falls back to a solid hairline at width 0 so the container 'stays framed' — which is why Toast, Modal and Bracketed panes keep a border when you set 0. Drop that fallback AND update the test that asserts it: `bracket_frame_zero_border_is_a_uniform_hairline_not_broken_corners` in heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs.\n\nNOTE: border now lives at `style.visual.border` after the Layout/Visual split (F003/P017/T1, commit 8718718) — re-verify the line references first.",
      "notes": "",
