    {
      "id": "efa9d4f8-7c3d-48dd-b6dd-6eea1d81248d",
      "phaseId": "0e4c21e5-1cf7-4c0a-a00e-76ffbef60703",
      "number": 341,
      "shortId": "XUV82",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "one-door-for-pointer-input-int",
      "title": "One door for pointer input into the app's widget trees, with a guard that reads the event loop",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "The host half of the same defect. T1 stops a CONTAINER dropping a kind; this stops the HOST never\nsending it. Both are needed: framework routing cannot deliver an event winit handed to nobody.\n\n## What was wrong (heca/src/app/events.rs, as of 2026-07-26)\n\nEach seam picked a different subset, and each looked reasonable in isolation:\n\n| seam | move | press | release | wheel |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| modal layer (app/events.rs:209, :251) | yes | yes | **no** | **no branch at all** |\n| chrome tree (chrome/mod.rs:3108, :3123) | yes | yes | yes | **no** |\n| pane header (chrome/mod.rs:1193, :1214) | yes | yes | **no** | **no** |\n| pane viewport (chrome/mod.rs:1231-1289) | yes | yes | yes | **no** |\n\nA modal is \"a panel of buttons\", so a wheel looked irrelevant and a release looked redundant. Then a\nmodal body held a scroll region.\n\n## Built (2026-07-26, uncommitted)\n\n- `chrome::dispatch_modal_pointer(state, &Event) -> bool` (heca/src/chrome/mod.rs) — one function,\n  `true` when a modal owns the pointer so the caller stops. A `debug_assert!` pins it to the pointer\n  kinds; keys go through the keymap.\n- `heca/src/app/events.rs`: `CursorMoved`, `MouseInput` (Pressed AND Released) and `MouseWheel` all\n  route through it. `wheel_event()` converts winit deltas to `Event::Scroll` using the showcase's\n  convention (LineDelta negated; PixelDelta / 20.0; Shift + a wheel with no native X remapped to X)\n  so a region scrolls identically in the app and the showcase.\n- `heca/tests/pointer_funnel.rs` — reads `app/events.rs` and fails when a pointer branch is handled\n  without the funnel, or when the button branch reaches it without deciding both Pressed and\n  Released. Verified against the pre-fix file: all three branches would have failed.\n\n## Remaining\n\n- The chrome tree, pane headers and pane viewport seams still hand-pick kinds. Fold them into the\n  same funnel shape (a `dispatch_chrome_pointer` / one router that resolves which retained tree owns\n  the pointer) and extend `pointer_funnel.rs` to cover them. Note `chrome_dispatch_press` DISCARDS\n  the tree afterwards (`state.chrome_tree = None`, chrome/mod.rs:3114) — a scroll region in the\n  sidebar cannot hold a grab across events at all while that stands. Decide it here.\n- `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:1274` `dispatch_pane_viewport_release` exists solely because this bug was\n  hit there earlier and patched locally; it should fall out of the shared path.\n\n## Done when\n\n- Every retained tree in the app receives move, press, release and wheel through one funnel.\n- `pointer_funnel.rs` covers every seam, and fails when one bypasses it.\n- The USER confirms in the app: wheel over a modal body scrolls it and does NOT scroll the terminal\n  behind; a thumb drag released anywhere stops; the sidebar and pane-header widgets still behave.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-26, driven by the user in the app.\n\n## Host delivery\n- `chrome::dispatch_modal_pointer` — one door to the modal layer; `CursorMoved`, `MouseInput`\n  (Pressed AND Released) and `MouseWheel` all go through it. `wheel_event()` matches the showcase's\n  delta + Shift-to-X convention.\n- `chrome_dispatch_release` / `chrome_dispatch_wheel` — the retained chrome tree gets the two kinds\n  it never had. The wheel is offered to the sidebar before the terminal.\n- `chrome_dispatch_press` now RETURNS whether a widget consumed it, and the left-sidebar path takes\n  that as final. That was the actual cause of \"dragging the thumb activates the pane\": a press was\n  resolved by geometry (`sidebar_drag_source`) before the widget tree ever saw it, and the thumb sits\n  inside the pane card's bounds.\n- **The tree is no longer discarded on press** (`chrome_tree = None` is gone). That line was a\n  rebuild used as a reset; nothing spanning two events could survive it. The drift it guarded is\n  handled by the signature rebuild + `sync_chrome_signals`.\n- Guards: `heca/tests/pointer_funnel.rs` now also requires the chrome tree's release and wheel.\n\n## The sidebar has a real ScrollRegion\nOffset lives in `SharedChromeState.workspaces.scroll` (the signal already reserved for it), restored\nvia `scroll_to` (reports `event: None`) and written back only when `event.is_some()` — so a rebuild\ncannot be mistaken for the user scrolling. The right sidebar gets the region without persistence; no\ncontainer state owns an offset for it yet.\n\n## Widget-level fixes that came out of the user's testing (all in heca-grid-ui, so every future\n## region gets them)\n- `Component::wants_visible` — default keyboard focus; `Row`/`MarkerGroup`/`DockFrame` add their nav\n  cursor. Any enclosing region scrolls to it, so `prefix+e` + j/k follows without a host call. It\n  tracks the target's NATURAL position, so it follows the selection and does not fight the wheel.\n- The scrollbar owns its whole lane for hover (`in_scrollbar_lane`, shared with the paging press), so\n  the row behind it no longer highlights.\n- `SCROLLBAR_EDGE_INSET` — the bar sits flush at the edge; the pad is clearance from content only.\n- **Per-side padding on `Layout`** (`padding_left/right/top/bottom`, cascade side → axis → uniform,\n  mirroring margins) + `LayoutExt` builders. Free in the declarative model, since the property\n  surface is `Layout`'s own fields.\n- `reserve_scrollbar_gutters` — the region reserves the lane in LAYOUT, so a card is laid out beside\n  the bar and keeps its rounded corner instead of being clipped flat. It takes `max(existing padding,\n  gutter)` rather than the sum, so where the padding is already roomy the bar sits in it and both\n  sides stay equal. Cannot oscillate: narrowing content only makes it taller.\n- `SCROLLBAR_W` 8 → 5 (visible thickness only; the 16px grab lane is unchanged).\n\n## Not done\nThe pane-header seam still hand-picks kinds (`dispatch_pane_header_press`/`_move`, no release). The\nuser's direction for it is \"fix it using the right widgets\" rather than patching another seam.",
